<title>GERMANY: East German May industry output rises 0.3 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>East German May industry output rises 0.3 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following indicator:</p>
<p>E.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    May 97     Apr 97	May 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)  +0.3	 +2.5	  +0.9</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.6	 +2.2	  +0.8</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     147.1	146.7	 144.8</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     May 97		  Apr 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   171.7	+0.9     170.1	 +2.1</p>
<p>Including:</p>
<p>  Intermediate goods    203.5	-1.1     205.8	 +4.7</p>
<p>  Capital goods	   131.7	-3.2     136.0	 -6.5</p>
<p> Energy output	     89.3	-0.7	89.9	 +7.4</p>
<p> Construction	     185.1	-0.5     186.1	 -0.8</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr-May 97 with Feb-Mar 97:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +4.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison May-Apr 97 with May-Apr 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +1.9</p>
<p> Mining					-3.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		   +9.5</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods	+15.0</p>
<p>		Capital goods		+3.4</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	  +9.0</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	     +6.9</p>
<p> Energy output			     -1.1</p>
<p> Construction				-9.9</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-28-26097150</p>
</text>
